Lane Warden Production Battle Slice
Build: P2-0.16.0
Design baseline: 1.7
Stable install scope: /lol-the-spire/lane-warden-prod-v0.10.4/
P2 Tactical Models: Living Lanes cohorts now render as phone-scale miniature formations baked from CC0 Quaternius glTF models. Warden, Ironjack, Slingline, enemy line, raider, and brute use distinct silhouettes, scale, palette, formation, facing, and motion language.
Cohort representation: simulation remains cohort-based; visual members are not separately simulated. Visible member count falls with cohort HP, fallen poses persist briefly, reinforcements arrive with an entry pulse, supporting cohorts show ranged intent, and slowed/reinforced/engaged states retain clear treatments.
Structures: Bastion, Guard, Gate, and one shared tower chassis use model-derived silhouettes. Tower function is identified through lightweight attachments. Siege Ram uses an original low-poly runtime chassis proxy with crew silhouettes.
Asset pipeline: untouched downloaded originals, deterministic processed sprite atlas, authoritative manifest, per-file hashes, licenses, source URLs, and transformation records are stored under assets/.
Commander and camera: constant spatial speed, tap-to-move, mid-move retarget/reversal, one-finger pan, pinch zoom, recenter, and lane focus remain unchanged from P2-0.15.3.
Combat, reward packets, progression, run persistence, encounter tuning, Reclamation, Last Stand, and deployment capacity are unchanged.
P2-0.15.1 delivery protections remain: explicit shell build marker, mixed-shell repair, stale-shell rejection, and build.json-last deployment discipline.
